    {
      "v": 7,
      "zh": "他对犹大人说：「我们要建造这些城邑，四围筑墙，盖楼，安门，做闩；地还属我们，是因寻求耶和华―我们的　神；我们既寻求他，他就赐我们四境平安。」于是建造城邑，诸事亨通。",
      "en": "He said to the people of Judah:[NOTE:1] “Let’s build these cities and fortify them with walls, towers, and barred gates.[NOTE:2] The land remains ours because we have followed[NOTE:3] the Lord our God; we have followed him, and he has made us secure on all sides.”[NOTE:4] So they built the cities[NOTE:5] and prospered.",
      "notes": [
        "The words “the people of” are supplied in the translation for clarification. The Hebrew text uses the name “Judah” by metonymy for the people of Judah.",
        "Heb “and we will surround [them] with wall[s] and towers, doors, and bars.”",
        "Heb “sought.”",
        "Heb “we sought him, and he has given us rest all around.”",
        "The words “the cities” are supplied in the translation for clarification and for stylistic reasons."
      ],
